><li>School recommendation program</li></ul><p>* After any applicable <a href="https://www.cdu.edu.au/study/essentials/study-pathways/pathways-study#apply-with-your-australian-tertiary-admission-ranking--atar-">adjustment factors</a> have been applied.</p><p>International applicants who have completed the CDU Foundation Studies Program or an equivalent program at another Australian institution, with a minimum of 65% in Foundation English Units A and B (or their equivalents), are eligible to apply.</p><p><strong>DOMESTIC STUDENTS</strong></p><p>To gain entry into Charles Darwin University, all Higher Education applicants must satisfy the University''s English Language Proficiency Requirements for their chosen course of study. All applicants will be required to supply evidence of this at the time of application.</p><p>The minimum English language requirement for this course can be met by evidencing of one of the following: </p><p><br/><strong>^ Minimum Requirements for English Tests:</strong></p><p><br/>IELTS One Skill Retake is accepted, allowing candidates to retake a single skill within 60 days of sitting their initial test. One Skill Retake results are valid for two years from the date of the first test (not from the date of the Retake test) to the date of commencement at CDU. </p><p>CDU accepts combined results from two test sittings of IELTS Academic, PTE Academic, or TOEFL, taken within a six-month period, if:</p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.cdu.edu.au/study/course/bachelor-computer-science-wcoms1',
    updated_at = NOW()
